On Fri, 7 Apr 2006, L wrote:
>
> This Monster Ring patch is a further developed version of Arthur J.
> O'Dwyer's Monster Ring patch, in which I've made:

I like it! :)

One sort-of-offtopic comment on the code itself: Why did you write this

+  for (i = W_RINGL; i; i = (i == W_RINGL ? W_RINGR : 0)) {
+      old = which_armor(mon, i);
+      if (old) update_mon_intrinsics(mon, old, TRUE, TRUE);
+  }

instead of this?

+  old = which_armor(mon, W_RINGL);
+  if (old) update_mon_intrinsics(mon, old, TRUE, TRUE);
+  old = which_armor(mon, W_RINGR);
+  if (old) update_mon_intrinsics(mon, old, TRUE, TRUE);

I guarantee you the latter will be faster on compilers where there's
any difference at all, and IMNSHO the latter is much clearer.

[...]
> * Player-monsters can now be generated with rings.

   Good idea, but your code there has a "vanishingly small" chance of
an infinite loop. Consider adding a loop counter so it only tries maybe
10 times before giving up, or rule out the "bad" rings to start with.
Also, I can't tell from a quick glance: you don't generate vortices
wearing rings, or anything silly like that, right? :)

[...]
> * Later: implement jumping for monsters (with special consideration in
> the case of player monster knights), then give it to unicorns to match
> their current jumpy behaviour.

   Wait... what does this have to do with rings? :)  I like the overhauled
monster-attribute macros, though; I suppose "jumping" would fit in as 
one of those bitflags.

   I'll link to your patch from my patch list.

